"n.ab.vip":"I like to say that my <em>conscious</em> dive into psychology and spirituality began with a magazine article in “Metropol” about a 10-day silent <strong>Vipassana</strong> retreat. I read it, got curious, went, and grasped nothing except the first of the three marks of existence: <strong>impermanence</strong>. I had it inscribed on my chest and drifted on into cognitive-behavioural lectures, behaviourism, philosophy and psychology.",
"n.ab.ther":"<strong>Individual psychotherapy</strong> is one of the best investments I’ve ever made. It helped me through a bottomless identity crisis, severe depression, war and emigration, and it keeps teaching me to live unforced and true to myself, in tune with the call of soul and body. I carry the value of this experience into the world through my coaching practice.",
"n.ab.conv":"My foundational belief comes from my teachers and my own experience: <strong>we can only change what we become aware of</strong>. Awareness of deep motivations, needs and biases is one of the key preconditions for the change we want.",
"n.ab.credo":"So my work is to help a person widen their space of <span class=\"term\" tabindex=\"0\">self-knowing<span class=\"tip\" role=\"tooltip\">A deep, whole understanding of your own essence, inner compass and hidden potential</span></span>",
