"n.ob.n":"In quantum physics there is the observer effect: the very act of measuring changes the state of a system. While a particle isn’t observed it behaves like a wave; once a detector appears, it “chooses” one path. Physicists stress that the observer is an instrument, not consciousness, so for me this is a metaphor. But an apt one: what we become aware of starts to change, and what stays outside our attention quietly runs us.",
"n.ob.h":"Hover or tap: where attention falls, the waves gather into lines",
"n.ob.a":"outside attention","n.ob.b":"in the field of attention",
